# TRIM reflection + EIRENE-faithful absorb-and-re-emit for D on a W wall.
#
# Channels are evaluated in order; cumulative probability accumulates per
# species; first channel to cross U~U[0,1] fires. Recommended ordering:
#     1) T ... (variable prob = R_N from TRIM table)
#     2) A ... (catch-all; prob=1; internally splits atom/molecule/pump)
#
# Species-agnostic: swap D->H, D2->H2, D_on_W->H_on_Li etc. for LTX.

# --- D+ recycling: neutralize + TRIM reflect as D, else EIRENE absorb-and-re-emit.
#     Returned fraction R=0.99; of those, 95% as D2, 5% as atomic D (EIRENE WTD defaults).
D+ --> D
T D_on_W

D+ --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

# --- D recycling: identical pipeline, incident species is atomic D.
D --> D
T D_on_W

D --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

# --- D2 recycling: no TRIM (molecules dissociate / don't reflect); simple absorb-and-return.
#     R=0.99, no f_mol needed because reactant == product.
D2 --> D2
A 0.99
